report += '\nThe frozen 15% primary gate passes; the 25% secondary gate fails at the palatal 0.40 mm group (30.38%). This is unfit-group interpolation within one published sensor setup, not independent specimen or patient validation. Qualitative plateau and some abstract values were known before fitting. [Elkholy et al., DOI 10.2319/011316-37R.1, Table 2](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8597333/); source image, calibration-only crop and full-table reading are preserved. An unused palatal 0.75 mm IQR metadata cell was initially misread; corrected metadata is recorded without altering frozen predictions.\n\nR3 keeps the source conditions and compares absolute palatal force at 0.25 mm. The same-study conversion gate passes (10.2%, 7.8% error); independent 2015 transfer fails (149.7%, 144.3%). Predicted 7.52/10.97 N versus independent measured 3.01/4.49 N. [2016 Table 1](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8597333/), [independent 2015 measurement, DOI 10.1007/s00056-015-0307-3](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26446503/). Different contralateral teeth, fixture, forming, retention, temperature and summary statistic may contribute; no single causal source is identified. The scalar effective intercept is a diagnostic, not a measured geometric gap.\n\n## Force window and relaxation\n\nThe 0.5–1.0 N range is a **descriptive fixed-appliance bodily-movement reference**, not a validated aligner or patient safety window. [Theodorou et al., DOI 10.1016/j.ajodo.2019.05.011](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ajodo.2019.05.011). At 0.20 mm, the literature-IQR scenarios place 17 simulated teeth above, 81 below, 63 across a boundary and 3 within that range. At 0.25 mm: 22 above, 73 below, 62 across and 7 within. Every physical classification is UNKNOWN because the force-transfer gate failed. No root, PDL, centre of resistance or biological exposure was measured.\n\nTensile coupon 37°C/3 h (79.62% retained stress), wet-bending coupon 37°C/24 h (4.17%) and unloaded saliva/dry aging are distinct records. No pooling, shared Prony fit or time interpolation is performed. `raw/RELAXATION_CASES.json` identifies each load case and explicitly flags unloaded aging as different from relaxation. Conditional rigid-ribbon scenarios are simulations only. [Tension study](https://doi.org/10.1186/s13005-025-00497-7), [wet bending](https://doi.org/10.3390/bioengineering9080349), [unloaded aging](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jds.2023.04.017).\n\n## Numerical controls, costs and remaining construction\n\nThe independent Hermite FE reproduces the same reduced-model wrenches to 6.82e−13; force balance to 1.01e−14 N and global torque to 9.21e−13 Nmm. Nonnegative endpoint fitting gives the same R2 response. These are same-information numerical controls and establish no algorithm superiority or physical accuracy. Intentional wrong stiffness/force/torque/thickness values reject under the same gates; R2 doubling the successful primary prediction fails.\n\nGeometry preparation: 6.73 s, peak process RSS 293 MiB, no source-tree or mesh copies. All computations stay below 4 threads and no GPU/heavy step is used. Full source discovery wall time and token cost are UNKNOWN; failures and measured preparation/query/fit costs are preserved in COSTS/COMMANDS. Lane output is below 10 MB and the 3 GB cap.\n\nA Bite2Text predicted 11–12 span of 0.789 mm creates a 259 N **artifact**; all frozen outputs are retained, not silently filtered. Source-labelled Teeth3DS and predicted Bite2Text diagnostics are separated. The next operation is matched forming/thickness, seated baseline and signed force-displacement measurements on the same specimens and arch. The lab port already refuses absent measurements (`NEEDS_MATCHED_MEASUREMENT`); no physical calibration is claimed. See MEASUREMENT_SPEC.md.\n'
